# build output
dist/
# astro generated types & cache
.astro/
# dependencies
node_modules/
# python venv. Used by two build/kit scripts:
#   • Civic Almanac build gate: schema/validate.py needs jsonschema (scripts/sync-almanac-data.mjs)
#   • Outreach kit QR codes: segno (scripts/gen-outreach-kit.py)
# One-time: python3 -m venv .venv && ./.venv/bin/pip install jsonschema segno
.venv/

# local preview scratch (temp copies served via the dev server, never committed)
public/_preview-*.html
# env & secrets (never commit AWS keys)
.env
.env.*
# os / editor
.DS_Store

# internal / infra / personal — keep local, never publish
AWS_SETUP.md
DEPLOY_RUNBOOK.md
HANDOFF_*.md

# The whole handoffs/ directory is internal. HANDOFF_*.md above already caught most
# of it, but SPINOFF-SEED_* files slipped past that pattern and were published: they
# carry local folder paths (~/Projects/...) and band/Level classification, the same
# private-tree exposure PORTFOLIO.md had. Ignore the directory so the next file added
# there cannot leak by naming convention. (2026-08-26)
handoffs/

# Internal tooling that reads the private portfolio manifest and scans sibling project
# folders. It cannot work from a clone and its dependency (PORTFOLIO.md) is not
# published, so shipping it only handed a forker a script that ENOENTs. (2026-08-26)
scripts/family-status.mjs

MCKL-redaction-license-email.md

# internal docs — never publish (added 2026-07-20)
TRASH-TRACKER-PLAN.md
PERSONAS-STRESS-TEST.md

# keep internal / infra out of the public repo (added 2026-07-20)
# infra/*.py IS tracked (deployed Lambda logic — no secrets); only the
# cred-touching setup scripts + build cruft stay local (updated 2026-08-07).
infra/*.sh
infra/__pycache__/

# private ANC accountability outputs — aggregated from private trash data, never publish
trash-metrics-out/

# Feedback inbox, review pages and verdict records (added 2026-08-25, roadmap 4.7).
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. Everything under here is what strangers typed into the feedback
# box on a civic site — it can contain their address, their landlord, their situation.
# It is pulled to this machine to be read and acted on, and it does not go any further.
# The verdicts change the roadmap; the words behind them stay here.
feedback-out/
FEEDBACK_REVIEW_*.md
APPROVED_feedback-verdicts_*.json

# The DNS watchdog moved to Agentic Environment on 2026-08-25 — it is a machine-level
# instrument, not an IPS concern. It lives at `Agentic Environment/scripts/check_dns.sh`
# and logs beside itself. Nothing to ignore here any more; this note is the signpost.
.owner
.project-id.json
_OWNED-BY-PERSONAL.md
_to_delete/

# Personal event prep — not site content
EVENT_KIT.md

# Local ops runbooks — may reference private addresses. Never publish.
.local-ops/

# Internal working docs — kept locally, not published.
# PORTFOLIO.md maps the private project tree; OUTREACH.md is a playbook addressed to Pippa.
PORTFOLIO.md
OUTREACH.md

# Findings written ABOUT this repo's own infrastructure. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC, and a document
# describing where the deploy is weak (no staging tier, a single bucket and distribution, a build
# that reads the working tree, and the variable that overrides the dirty-tree guard) is not
# something to hand the internet about a live civic site. Same treatment as AWS_SETUP.md and
# DEPLOY_RUNBOOK.md above: kept locally, read by whoever fixes it, never published. (2026-09-03)
FINDING_*
